%% Option C with the settings that worked (docs/50-option-c-wildcard-certificate.md, Figure 4).
%% Text source only. The figure shown in the docs is docs/diagrams/option-c/option-c-wildcard-cert.*.png.
flowchart LR
    subgraph YOU["You: workstation + enterprise CA"]
        K["1. One key, one CSR<br/>SAN DNS:*.&lt;NODE_DOMAIN&gt;<br/>2. the CA signs it, valid 2 years"]
        R["Every 2 years: renew<br/>steps 1-3 with a new key<br/>each node reboots once; NNCP and NAS unchanged"]
    end
    subgraph CL["Cluster"]
        MC["MachineConfig 99-&lt;pool&gt;-ipsec-wildcard-cert<br/>ca.pem + left_server.p12 + import unit"]
        C1["C1: one NNCP for the pool<br/>leftid %fromcert, left %defaultroute"]
        C2["C2: Kyverno GeneratingPolicy<br/>one NNCP per node, leftid @&lt;node&gt;<br/>restart after a change"]
    end
    subgraph NODE["Every node of the pool"]
        IMP["4. Reboots once; imports left_server<br/>at boot, before libreswan"]
        CON["Connection ipsec-nas<br/>every node presents CN=ocp-ipsec-workers, O=KCS"]
    end
    subgraph NAS["NAS: settings that worked, for C1 and C2"]
        S["rightid=%fromcert: identity from the certificate<br/>uniqueids=no: several peers, one identity<br/>rightca: the enterprise root; firewall: worker subnet<br/>NFS accepted only through IPsec"]
    end
    K -- "3. checked, bundled" --> MC
    MC -- MCO --> IMP
    IMP --> CON
    C1 -- NMState --> CON
    C2 -- NMState --> CON
    CON <-- "IKEv2 + ESP" --> S
